266
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:55,451
We don't eat animals with fur, by the way.

267
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:59,637
I'm not complaining, but why are
you throwing us this huge party?

268
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:01,200
A friend of our saviors.

269
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:03,091
is a friend of ours, too.

270
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:04,280
Saviors, huh?

271
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:06,209
They need the whole story.

272
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,840
Hey, Brooke!

273
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:26,820
Oh, Joy, I read about your big battle.

274
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,760
I'm so glad you're all OK.

275
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:30,757
I missed you.

276
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:31,720
What's wrong?

277
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,195
You're all banged up.

278
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,130
Never mind me.

279
00:15:34,213 --> 00:15:35,560
I'm sorry about Sanji.

280
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:37,900
I feel like I've lost all face.

281
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:40,780
Not that I have one to begin with.

282
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:42,050
Oh, hey.

283
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:44,397
Wasn't Momo supposed to
be with you guys, too?

284
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:46,380
Yes, and he's unharmed.

285
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:52,380
But the thing is, he's not very
fond of the makes. Well, why not?

286
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:54,040
They're so nice to us.

287
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:57,691
That's true, but he's decided
to lock himself up in a room.

288
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:00,300
Still, that's convenient for us. Huh?

289
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:02,277
Could you explain that better?

290
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:04,437
Because you're not making any sense.

291
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,108
Just come this way, please.

292
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:10,320
Hey, all newcomers to Zoe, huddle up.

293
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:14,260
First off, where did Kinemun go?

294
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:17,148
We got split up, but
he should be here soon.

295
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:18,340
Well, that's fine.

296
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:20,197
Yeah, it'll work out nicely.

297
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:26,360
While we're here, please do not mention
the land of Wano or samurai either.

298
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,200
Better not risk it.

299
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:32,260
It might cause offense to the minks.

300
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:34,160
Or pain more accurately.

301
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:37,700
It might even make them hate you.

302
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:39,140
Make them hate us?

303
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:41,460
Okay, but what's the deal?

304
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:43,505
What's wrong with the samurai?

305
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:46,738
There's something about this
country you didn't know.

306
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:54,300
So you thought you could get away.

307
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,200
But you can't run now.

308
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:02,080
Come here, barren corpse.

309
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,380
What's that for?

310
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:05,240
A corpse?

311
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:11,597
Once U-T-O reach right flank, that's
where you'll find your crew's corpse.

312
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:12,621
We'll find what?

313
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:18,636
So when she said there was a corpse,
she was just talking about Brooke.

314
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:21,860
We call him that as a term of endearment.

315
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,357
Kind of misleading, don't you think?

316
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:26,177
Such a lovely surprise.

317
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:29,460
I've never seen such an
alluring creature before.

318
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:38,495
Dog mains can't resist chewing a bone.

319
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,200
What can I say?

320
00:17:40,620 --> 00:17:41,880
Fine, whatever.

321
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:48,580
Luffy, I don't see Traffy. Is he here?

322
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:52,540
Yeah, he said Bear Place. He's fine.

323
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:55,351
Instead, we should worry more about Sanji.

324
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,720
He left you a letter, didn't he?

325
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,717
This thing will work
out one way or another.

326
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:02,630
Hmm.

327
00:18:02,713 --> 00:18:03,880
He wasn't kidnapped.

328
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:04,937
He just left.

329
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:06,377
That's what I'm worried about!

330
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,401
The whole thing is way too fishy!

331
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:10,297
I'm so sorry. We...

332
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,640
we couldn't do anything to stop him!

333
00:18:13,380 --> 00:18:15,980
Hey, you don't need to cry. Yeah.

334
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:17,420
I mean, maybe?

335
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:21,037
Honestly, I don't know if it's
something to cry about or not.

336
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:24,597
What I'm saying is you need to give us
some more details, because I'm lost.

337
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:25,560
No kidding.

338
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:28,017
Last I heard, Big Mom's ship was there.

339
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:31,037
But I don't know what happened
next or how you guys got away.

340
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:33,937
Then it's a giant elephant
and talking animal people

341
00:18:34,020 --> 00:18:37,196
and something bad happened
and the city got destroyed.

342
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,677
And I thought the Mink
tribe was our enemy.

343
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,936
But we got here and they all love us.

344
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:45,557
We're friends of their
saviors, they're telling me.

345
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:46,470
Listen, Nami.

346
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:48,840
We need to hear the details in full.

347
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:52,837
Tell us everything that's
happened in the past 11 days.

348
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:55,391
since you left Dressrosa aboard the Sunny.

349
00:18:56,980 --> 00:18:58,040
I'm sorry.

350
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,635
This whole situation has me worked up.

351
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:04,180
Okay, I'll tell you
everything that happened.

352
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:08,893
First, we ran into trouble when we
were barely off the coast of Dressrosa.

353
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:14,260
The Big Mom Pirates appeared on
a huge singing ship. Singing?

354
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:17,880
Shipping, shipping!

355
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:24,497
We were able to spot
the two members of her

356
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:27,404
crew that Luthi ran into
back on Fishman Island.

357
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:30,640
Mama, confirming that
we have located Caesar.

358
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:35,861
Let us send them on our bon voyage by seeking
their ship to recover Monsieur Caesar.

359
00:19:36,660 --> 00:19:38,460
But they had company.

360
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:44,280
A fellow member of the worst generation,

361
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:52,260
Capone gang veggie seems like his
crew is working under Big Mom now?

362
00:19:52,780 --> 00:19:55,780
They came for Caesar,
but it wasn't a rescue.

363
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:57,900
In fact, he was terrified

364
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:02,401
Although it's not like we
could escape either way.

365
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:06,437
So even if it was crazy, we
needed to do something in a hurry!

366
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:08,755
Let's use a coup de burst to run away!

367
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,397
What about the gout cannon?

368
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:12,657
We don't have enough spare cola for that.

369
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:14,681
I got a different plan this time.

370
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:18,160
Whatever your plan is, hurry up!

371
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:21,460
If you don't want them to
take you, then play nice!

372
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:25,837
Okay, Brooke, we're gonna fight him
from the stern and create an opening.

373
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:26,750
Roger.

374
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,400
Welcome to the Soul Parade!

375
00:20:41,660 --> 00:20:43,880
Chopper Robin, is that really you?

376
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:45,560
Here he comes. Ready?

377
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:53,280
I do not approve of this bad one bit!

378
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:55,880
You will pay for this.

379
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:58,617
Some audacity treating me like a bag!

380
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:01,197
Will you stop resisting us?

381
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,560
We're trying to save you.

382
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:18,860
Thank you, Chopper. Nice bitch.

383
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,920
He can fly?

384
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:26,660
Here we go.

385
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,180
Well, a prayer!

386
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,080
Spectre!

387
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:39,920
A room cannibals in our way!

388
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:50,540
The starbursts take a service, damn it!

389
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:52,260
My turn, now!

390
00:21:52,820 --> 00:21:53,920
Climb intact!

391
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,520
Weather!

392
00:21:56,340 --> 00:21:57,180
Tag!

393
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:00,440
Come hatch!

394
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:02,140
K-Club!

395
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:21,880
We're going to lose
them! What should we do?

396
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:27,980
Don't you guys really kick some ass?

397
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:31,500
That doesn't make me blush at all.

398
00:22:31,780 --> 00:22:33,760
That was on the edge of my seat.

399
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:37,720
New bird teamwork! You're
so clever. Oh, stop.

400
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:39,737
I know I'm awesome, but please.

401
00:22:39,820 --> 00:22:44,217
So you came here after that how
long did it take so was close

402
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:48,020
to us at the time luckily we
made it here the very next day

403
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,380
So we've been here ten days.

404
00:22:51,660 --> 00:22:53,542
I have a question about the city

405
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:57,457
It looked like the oldest sign of
destruction was from about two weeks ago,

406
00:22:57,540 --> 00:23:00,716
so the incident was over by
the time everyone arrived.

407
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:02,670
That's correct.

408
00:23:02,753 --> 00:23:07,520
When we found your friends here, most of
our country had already been destroyed.

409
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:09,357
Despite that,

410
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:14,317
their arrival was nothing short of a
miracle for our people without their help.

411
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:15,277
We'd be lost.

412
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:19,737
We owe them for their courage and
for choppers medical expertise.

413
00:23:19,820 --> 00:23:25,637
Everyone here in the mokumo
dukedom was nearly wiped out.

414
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:32,597
I know the

415
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,510
wounds are still

416
00:23:33,593 --> 00:23:34,423
pretty fresh on this whole?

417
00:23:34,506 --> 00:23:37,912
So if you don't want to talk
about it, I'm okay with that.

418
00:23:38,380 --> 00:23:40,300
No, we're allies now.

419
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:41,815
You two need to know.

420
00:23:41,980 --> 00:23:44,921
I will tell you everything
that happened that day.

421
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:46,840
Hey! Everybody!

422
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:51,660
The Duke is awake!

423
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:54,760
I can't believe it!

424
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:57,250
Finally!

425
00:23:57,333 --> 00:23:58,163
Emily!

426
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:04,580
Duke Dogstorm, I was so worried.

427
00:24:06,500 --> 00:24:09,317
OK, I'll give him a checkup
and see what he needs.

428
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,640
Tristan, Miyagi, let's go! Whoa!

429
00:24:12,220 --> 00:24:13,180
On my way!

430
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:14,740
Boy, oh boy!

431
00:24:14,940 --> 00:24:17,116
I have got to see the master at work!

432
00:24:18,020 --> 00:24:18,860
Please, Dr.

433
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:20,216
Miyagi, wait for me!

434
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:27,160
Oh, hey, I almost forgot.

435
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:30,909
Duke Dog Storm said he'd like
to meet with our saviors ASAP.

436
00:24:31,460 --> 00:24:32,297
Right, got it.

437
00:24:32,380 --> 00:24:34,968
Will Yuti and your crew
please come with me?

438
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:36,480
Okay, whatever.

439
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:38,100
But who's this dog?

440
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:43,500
He is the leader of the Mokumo
Dukedom, meaning the ruler of all Zo.

441
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:48,877
He was hurt badly in the attack, and
unfortunately he's been in a coma ever since.

442
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:50,480
Same as our other leader.

443
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:52,630
Huh?

444
00:24:52,713 --> 00:24:54,240
You've got two? Indeed.

445
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:57,140
It may seem strange, but this is our way.

446
00:24:58,560 --> 00:25:01,640
There is the King of
the Day, Duke Dogstorm.

447
00:25:02,580 --> 00:25:06,320
And the King of the
Night, Master Cat Viper.

448
00:25:40,740 --> 00:25:43,300
Oh, hey, I heard the news.

449
00:25:43,440 --> 00:25:45,260
Nice job beating Doflamingo.

450
00:25:45,780 --> 00:25:48,660
Well, it was really Straw Hat who did it.

451
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:50,517
Let's catch up back at the base.

452
00:25:50,600 --> 00:25:51,920
This way, Captain.

453
00:25:53,180 --> 00:25:54,010
Sure.

454
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:03,980
Then, in an instant, it
all came crashing down.

455
00:26:05,940 --> 00:26:09,940
The incident began 17
days ago, to be exact.

456
00:26:10,460 --> 00:26:13,695
A month and a half after
Beppo and his friends arrived,

457
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:17,940
the visitor spell rang out across
the Mokumo dukedom once more.

458
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:21,725
Except this time, it
wasn't the welcoming bell.

459
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:24,979
Rather, it was a sound we
hoped we would never hear.

460
00:26:25,080 --> 00:26:26,140
The raiding bell.

461
00:26:32,840 --> 00:26:34,477
That's not the welcoming bell.

462
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:36,040
It's the raiding bell.

463
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:37,710
The what?

464
00:26:38,100 --> 00:26:41,060
A young lady like you,
Karoo, wouldn't know.

465
00:26:41,480 --> 00:26:43,774
It's never been wrong in your lifetime.

466
00:26:43,940 --> 00:26:45,337
A bunch of pirates broke down the gate!

467
00:26:45,420 --> 00:26:47,126
Everybody get ready to fight!

468
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:51,400
Trampling down the forest on the
way, they invaded our peaceful city.

469
00:26:52,780 --> 00:26:57,080
Feeling such a huge disturbance on
its back, Zunesha let out a roar.

470
00:27:04,040 --> 00:27:05,340
So who were they?

471
00:27:05,540 --> 00:27:07,481
What did they even want from you?

472
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:11,760
They wanted something that
we could not give to them.

473
00:27:12,140 --> 00:27:13,780
Something we didn't have.

474
00:27:14,260 --> 00:27:16,260
Our pleas fell on deaf ears.

475
00:27:20,520 --> 00:27:24,040
You're hiding a warrior
from the land of Wano here.

476
00:27:24,280 --> 00:27:27,751
Now hand over Race or we will
smash this country to pieces!
